.TH DSLITE-B4.TOML 5 "August 2026" "dslite-b4 0.1.1" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
dslite-b4.toml \- configuration for the dslite-b4 daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/dslite-b4.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file uses TOML syntax.
Unknown fields are rejected.
The daemon should be run only after
.B dslite-b4 check-config
accepts the file.
.SH LOGGING
.TP
.B logging.level
Minimum log level.
Accepted values are
.BR error ,
.BR warn ,
.BR info ,
.BR debug ,
and
.BR trace .
The default is
.BR info .
The
.B RUST_LOG
environment variable takes precedence.
.SH RUNTIME STATE
.TP
.B runtime.state_dir
Directory for the locked PID file, runtime AFTR override, and status snapshot.
The default is
.B /run/dslite-b4
on Linux and
.B /var/run/dslite-b4
on illumos.
.SH TUNNEL
.TP
.B tunnel.name
Name of the managed tunnel interface.
The default is
.BR dslite0 .
Platform interface naming rules apply.
.TP
.B tunnel.local_v6
Local IPv6 tunnel endpoint.
When omitted, the kernel selects the source address for the route to the AFTR.
.TP
.B tunnel.local_v4
Local B4 IPv4 address.
The value must be a host address from 192.0.0.2 through 192.0.0.6 as reserved by RFC 6333.
The default is 192.0.0.2.
.TP
.B tunnel.mtu
Optional interface MTU.
When omitted, the operating system tunnel default is used.
.TP
.B tunnel.encapsulation_limit
Optional IPv6 encapsulation limit from 1 through 255.
The value
.B disabled
turns limit insertion off.
When omitted, the operating system tunnel default is used.
.SH AFTR
.TP
.B aftr.address
Optional static AFTR IPv6 address or DNS name.
A static value takes precedence over a runtime value and automatic discovery.
.SH DISCOVERY
.TP
.B discovery.method
Automatic discovery method.
Accepted values are
.B none
and
.BR hb46pp .
The default is
.BR none .
.TP
.B discovery.vendor_id
Six digit hexadecimal Broadband Forum vendor identifier sent by HB46PP.
The default is 000000.
.TP
.B discovery.product
Product identifier sent by HB46PP.
The default is
.BR dslite-b4 .
.TP
.B discovery.allow_unauthenticated
Allow HB46PP policy
.BR t=a ,
which permits HTTP or HTTPS without certificate validation.
The default is false.
Enable this only when required by the provider.
.SH HEALTH
.TP
.B health.interval_secs
Maximum number of seconds between reconciliation passes.
Network changes and runtime state changes can wake the daemon sooner.
The default is 30.
.TP
.B health.aftr_missing_grace_secs
Time to retain the current AFTR after it disappears from DNS results.
The default is 600 seconds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/dslite-b4.toml
Default configuration path.
.TP
.B /run/dslite-b4
Default Linux runtime state directory.
.TP
.B /var/run/dslite-b4
Default illumos runtime state directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dslite-b4 (8),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR smf (7)
